# Template for devops/backup/.env-media-mirror (gitignored).
#
#   cp devops/backup/.env-media-mirror-example devops/backup/.env-media-mirror
#   bash devops/minio/media-svcacct.sh production    # fills the values below
#   bash devops/secrets.sh minio minio-media-mirror devops/backup/.env-media-mirror
#
# Feeds the `minio-media-mirror` secret in the `minio` namespace, consumed by
# devops/backup/minio-media-mirror.yaml. See documentation/backups.md and
# documentation/secrets.md.
#
# Only the SOURCE lives here. The target GCS bucket is written under Workload
# Identity, so there is no target credential to hold.
#
# NEVER put a real credential in a committed file.

# This cluster's MinIO, as the read-only `media-backup` service account
# provisioned from the checked-in devops/minio-media-backup-policy.json. Get +
# List on the media bucket; a separate identity from media-proxy's reader
# because the mirror needs s3:ListBucket and the public read path must never
# have it.
#
# Do not fill these by hand -- run the script, so the credential in the cluster
# and the policy in the repo cannot drift.
SOURCE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
SOURCE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
